-- Source module: Solutions.P8LiftIface
/-!
# A restricted Proposition 8 interface (only the paper's cheap local operations)

`Butterfly.Prop8Iface` allows an arbitrary matrix as a non-recursive step, which makes it
vacuous. Here the non-recursive steps are restricted to the operations of §3.5/§5.1, each
of which touches every state entry a bounded number of times:

* `gate G` — a pointwise scalar gate across roles at equal addresses (`G` on the roles,
  identity on the addresses);
* `rowAdd w i j` — a binary row addition `x(j,c) += x(i,c)` (all columns `c`) on the address
  bits of role `w`, i.e. an address permutation;
* `phase w k₀ k₁ a` — the diagonal phase `i^{k₀ + k₁|κ| + Σ_{(r,c)} a_r x(r,c)}` on role `w`
  (covers `Z_u` with `a = 2u`, `S` on selected bits, scalars `i^{27|κ|}`);
* `perm σ` — a permutation of the roles;
* `child w h fwd` — a recursive call on slot `h` of role `w` (forward or the (17) inverse).

The step list is independent of the column type `κ` (the same program for every `κ`).

* `Prop8IfaceR.toIface`: the forgetful map to `Butterfly.Prop8Iface` (so `recOp_eq`,
  `recCost_le`, `prop14_output` apply).
* `den_row_card_le`: every local step's matrix has at most `|R|` nonzero entries per row
  (`≤ 1` except for gates), so one local step costs `≤ W · V` entry operations.
* `recCostR_le`: the §5.3 bound for the recursion whose local work is the actual work
  `≤ nloc · W · V` of the local steps (`nloc` = number of local steps, independent of `κ`).
-/

